WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for staticos-tour.mp4. The spoken lines were transcribed with whisper.cpp
(base.en model, speech-detection on) and tidied by reading; the cue times follow where
each word starts in the audio and can be a second out.

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:04.300
This is StaticOS, a whole computer

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.000
running right in your browser.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.700
It's a real desktop.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:10.100
Open apps, drag windows around,

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.700
and use the dock, all in one tab.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.400
Static Play has hundreds of games.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.800
Press Play, and it just runs.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.300
Nothing to download.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.100
There are over 60 apps,

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:26.600
and the launcher keeps every one

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.400
of them a quick search away.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:32.300
In Static Forge, you describe a game,

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.000
and AI builds it for you.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.700
Then jump into Static Studio

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.200
and edit every object

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.900
right down to the code.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:43.600
There's even a console-style hub

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:44.900
for cloud gaming.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.900
StaticOS, open it in any browser

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:54.000
at staticos.surge.sh.
